"{\"summary\":\"Commit e6a3304945597de51dc7020fc47bec49e3973ea1 (\\\"⚡ Skip rebuilds that move nothing and share reused vector blocks\\\") is the one that introduced the skip: it adds `change_set_moves_anything` and, in `rebuild_index`, returns `current` with zero counts when `changed_paths` is not None and the change set moves nothing. The same commit's message states a watcher change set that moves nothing now keeps the served generation instead of writing a copy of it.\",\"ranges\":[[429,472],[443,454],[455,472]]}"